Patch 0016. Three failures in a row had the same shape: a fact stated in two
places, one of them updated. This patch fixes the three, and then removes the
shape.

A TEST CREATED A REAL FLY APP

tests/test_deploy_script.py put a fake binary named `fly` on PATH and trusted the
script to find it. The script resolved `command -v flyctl` first, found the REAL
flyctl in the Codespace, and ran `fly apps create test-engine` against a live
Fly.io account — visible in the run as "automatically selected personal
organization". Six tests then failed because the app it had just created existed.

A test that touches production is a worse bug than the one it was written to
catch. Fixed three ways: FLY_BIN names the binary explicitly, the fake is
installed under both `fly` and `flyctl`, and _assert_fake() refuses to run unless
the binary the script will use is the one the test wrote. A regression test puts a
loud decoy flyctl earlier on PATH and proves it is never called. And with FLY_BIN
set the script no longer offers to install flyctl — a CI job that silently
downloads a real one is one step from a test that uses it.

  If a stray app remains:  fly apps destroy test-engine

AN EUR 18,000 PURCHASE WOULD HAVE GENERATED A DENSITY SCREEN

The intake route branched inline: kind === "envelope_study_deposit" ? "study" :
"screen". A Procurement Specification purchase fell through to "screen". The
client pays for one document and receives another, and nothing in the system
objects. The endpoint now comes from the catalogue (deliverableEndpoint), an
unmapped kind fails loudly with the intake preserved, and renderDeliverable
handles "spec" — returning the response schedule in the working-files slot, since
that is the artefact that makes four quotations comparable.

THE PROCUREMENT SPECIFICATION WAS PRICED, DOCUMENTED AND UNBUYABLE

The engagement ladder was a hand-written array of ids inside a component. Adding a
product to the catalogue and forgetting that one line left it invisible. The
ladder is now derived from a `surface` field that every product must declare —
with no default, so something unsellable has to be declared unsellable on purpose
— and a test fails if a literal ORDER array reappears.

THE SHAPE, REMOVED

tests/test_stack_consistency.py asserts the joins rather than the parts: every
product reaches a surface; every deliverable reaches an endpoint; every endpoint
the site names exists on the engine; every engagement the engine quotes can be
paid for; every paid route is metered and agent-reachable (/v1/deck the one
deliberate exception, named as deliberate); the published tools.json matches the
engine's live schemas and rates; the README names every product and every package;
the commercial spine lists what is actually purchasable; and every CLI command
appears in the runbook. Adding a command without documenting it now fails the
build. It is meant to.

THE UPSELL THE STUDY ALREADY CREATES

A delivered study ends with a constraint and a date, and somebody then has to buy
the thing that relieves it. /deliverable/<token> now offers the Procurement
Specification by name — reading the binding constraint out of the working files
the engine just produced, so it says "now somebody has to buy the thing that
relieves rack feed / tap-off rating" rather than a generic sentence. Shown after
the working files, never before: an upsell that arrives ahead of the evidence
reads as the point of the document.

`gridforge spec` with no --constraint now targets the same relief that
`spec --list` prints at the top. A tool that disagrees with itself between two
commands is worse than one that picks badly.

THE README DESCRIBED A DIFFERENT COMPANY

It called this repository "a marketing + lead-generation site" for a
"physics-informed energy management system" practice — four patches after it had
stopped being that. Rewritten: the honesty kernel, the product ladder, the engine,
the machine interface, the site map, what is deliberately absent. Two tests keep
it true.

docs/00_COMMERCIAL_SPINE.md goes to v0.2: the ladder now reflects what is built,
and the two durable assets are named — the cost library and the accuracy record.
Neither can be bought, scraped or inferred, and both accrue one hall at a time.

TESTS

21 new (310 total). CI gained a consistency job in `test` and a catalogue check in
`site`, so a drift of this class cannot reach main again.

